---
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const install = `# with uv (from a checkout)
uv sync

# or pip
pip install ci-doctorr

# or the self-contained image
docker run --rm ci-doctor:latest --version`;

const tryIt = `# Replay a captured log offline — no network, no LLM:
ci-doctor analyze --from-file failing-job.log

# Against a live pipeline (reads $CI_PIPELINE_ID etc. in CI):
ci-doctor analyze "$CI_PIPELINE_ID"`;
---
<Base title="Overview">
  <img class="hero-logo light" src="/ci-doctor-logo.svg" alt="ci-doctor — root-cause analysis for CI/CD" />
  <img class="hero-logo dark" src="/ci-doctor-logo-dark.svg" alt="ci-doctor — root-cause analysis for CI/CD" />
  <p class="pill">read-only · air-gap friendly · GitLab + GitHub</p>
  <h1>Know <em>why</em> your pipeline failed.</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    ci-doctor is a postmortem CI step that runs only when a pipeline fails, pulls the
    failed jobs' logs, works out where and why they broke, and emits a structured report —
    to the job log, to <code>report.md</code>/<code>report.json</code>, and optionally as a
    single idempotent note on the merge/pull request.
  </p>

  <div class="btn-row">
    <a class="btn primary" href="/usage/">Get started</a>
    <a class="btn" href="/cicd/">CI/CD examples</a>
    <a class="btn" href="/configuration/">Configuration</a>
  </div>

  <h2>The core idea</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Deterministic code decides <em>where</em> the job failed; the LLM only explains <em>why</em>.</strong>
    Phase attribution is a pure function of job metadata and log structure, computed before any
    model is called — so a loud, non-fatal cache-restore warning can never get blamed over the
    real <code>exit code 1</code> in your script. If the classifier is wrong, that's a bug with a
    failing test, not a prompt to tune.
  </p>

  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Never masks the failure</h3>
      <p>Read-only and always exits 0 — it can't change your pipeline's status or hide the real error.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Works with no LLM</h3>
      <p>Deterministic report out of the box: phase, reason, terminal command, evidence, remediation.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Bring your own model</h3>
      <p>Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint via <code>api_base</code> — Ollama, vLLM, llama.cpp, an internal gateway.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Air-gapped</h3>
      <p>No runtime downloads, no telemetry, no hardcoded hosts. Ship as a Docker image or offline wheels.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <Code code={install} lang="bash" theme="github-dark" />

  <h2>Try it</h2>
  <Code code={tryIt} lang="bash" theme="github-dark" />

  <div class="note">
    New here? <a href="/requirements/">Requirements</a> covers what it needs, then
    <a href="/configuration/">Configuration</a> and <a href="/cicd/">CI/CD Examples</a> get it
    running in your pipeline.
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero-logo { width: 100%; max-width: 460px; height: auto; margin: 0 0 1.75rem; }
  .hero-logo.light { display: block; }
  .hero-logo.dark { display: none; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    .hero-logo.light { display: none; }
    .hero-logo.dark { display: block; }
  }
</style>
